    "title": "Latto Returns To Social Media, Sparks Pregnancy Rumors With Cryptic Post",
    "text": "Big Momma is back! Latto is making her return to social media, but she’s not coming empty-handed. The rapper recently dropped off a teaser trailer for something new she’s been working on. That said, fans aren’t sure if it’s a new track or a pregnancy announcement. The trailer begins with what appears to be Latto walking toward a lion cub and feeding them a bottle of milk. “I ain’t go missing,” Latto says in the trailer. “I had to give y’all time to miss me. Before you run the game, you gotta take baby steps to go the distance. Home to the studio, studio back home, listening to every beat, feeling every kick. Ever since I was a little girl, I always dreamed of having my own. Big Momma. But this time the stakes way bigger. Now it’s on me to deliver.” The video fades to black, and the word “Midnight” appears. A clear signal that whatever the announcement may be, it’s coming soon. The rapper’s comment section was filled with celebrities and fans alike, who offered her encouragement, as well as their own conclusions on what Latto has planned. Yung Mimai hopped in the comments to show Latto some love, writing, “ let’s go!!!” Mariah The Scientist appeared to be enthralled with the visual, particularly the lion club. “It is a pleasant surprise hearing ur voice come down my timeline. Is that a baby cheetah? Where u get that from?” she wrote, whereas a fan claimed, “We knew you was pregnant .” Another fan commented, “Just say it, we already know.” Latto Pranks Followers With Surprise ‘Pregnancy’ Post Rumors began swirling that Latto was pregnant last month. The rapper did respond to the allegations, but not the way one would expect. Instead of offering clarification, the rapper opted for a more humorous route. In a short video posted to her Instagram Story, the rapper appeared, rocking a prosthetic baby bump, which only further fueled the allegations she has a bun in the oven. When The Neighborhood Talk reposted the clip, commenters quickly filled in their own interpretations. “She learned from Bardi. She’s actually pregnant and trying to throw ppl off. Congrats mam!” one user wrote. Another added, “Last time I played about being pregnant I really was so I don’t play like that no more,” while a third commented, “She just want to see how we feel about it first.” The range of responses illustrated how firmly the rumor had taken hold. Latto and 21 Savage have long been the subject of relationship speculation, though they confirmed their status publicly in 2025. In a September interview with TMZ, she referred to him simply as “my man.” Their professional paths have crossed as well; on his song “POP IT,” she delivers the line, “F*cking on this British man / Crib look like the Buckingham.” The collaboration blurred personal and professional boundaries in a way that often invites scrutiny.",
